+
+## YourBuddy integration
+
+YourBuddy sets `presentation: slot` to render the bottom workbench in `workbench.core`; `portal` retains upstream placement. Registered cards remain visible but disabled before a Session exists. Explicit user opens can reveal the target reader; background opens preserve the current document and workbench focus. PDF and Office documents use the native readers without replacing the Files tree. The terminal adapter uses DSH's terminal factory and retains each tab for the lifetime of its workbench record.
+
+The [rebuild recipe](../../scripts/rebuild-better-sidebar.mjs) uses the release's pinned source and dependency lock, current workspace service owners, and upstream build commands. It compares two clean output trees in an owned staging directory and does not replace this snapshot automatically. Source and archive identities and replayable product patches are recorded in [YOURBUDDY_UPSTREAM.json](./YOURBUDDY_UPSTREAM.json).
